   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Wan 2.1 I2V renders one clip per shot. Shot Video Engine is the switch in front of the video stage: wire other branches (MiniMax H3, or an API node such as Kling / Seedance / Hailuo) into its other inputs and pick one; only the chosen branch runs."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653",
   "title": "Note: 2 · Shot Video Engine: Wan branch"
  },
  {
   "id": 47,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    30,
    1822
   ],
   "size": [
    900,
    173
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 46,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Shot Video QA checks every clip offline (frozen, flicker, jumps, drift from the keyframe, melting regions) and with Gemini (use_llm). Failed shots get a new prompt and seed; the reroll branch renders only those, and Clip Reroll Merge puts them back. When every clip passes, the reroll branch never runs.\nAPI keys: set them as environment variables before starting ComfyUI, never in the workflow. GEMINI_API_KEY (or GOOGLE_API_KEY), ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ELEVENLABS_API_KEY."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653",
   "title": "Note: 3 · Shot Video QA and reroll"
  },
  {
